<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    DO NOT REMOVE com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars.

    On macOS 26.5, tccd refuses to show ANY Calendar prompt for a hardened-runtime binary
    that lacks this entitlement. The log reads:

        Prompting policy for hardened runtime; service: kTCCServiceCalendar
        requires entitlement com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars
        but it is missing. Policy disallows prompt, access denied.

    The failure is SILENT and PERMANENT. The re-prompt is policy-blocked while every
    authorization-status API still reports green. This entitlement is unrestricted: no
    provisioning profile and no special notarization are required.

    Note for editors: XML comments may not contain a double hyphen. AMFI's entitlement
    parser rejects the whole file if one appears, with only a line number to go on.

    Source: incident notes in PsychQuant/che-ical-mcp Entitlements.plist (MIT). Reasoning
    adopted as an idea; no code copied.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
